feat(payment): the payment ledger joins — intent, confirm, and the bridge into the trade machine

Three services in one drop: PaymentTransactionService (8 RPCs — the
ledger plus the intent/confirm faces), PaymentRefundService (6), and
PaymentChannelConfigService (3 read faces; the credentials leave the
responses with only the credentials_configured flag). The golden DDL
grows the three tables.

The confirm face is the bridge into the trade machine: the
transaction walks PENDING to SUCCEEDED (the transition guard makes
the replay a FailedPrecondition — the ledger's idempotency is the
state machine's), and the owning order walks PENDING_PAYMENT to PAID
through mark_order_paid (its replay stays silent — already-PAID is a
no-op, the ledger replay never double-walks the order). The intent
face materializes a PENDING transaction off the channel config
(disabled channels refuse) and answers the transaction message plus
the channel (the real channels plug their SDKs in place of the mock
trade-no) plus the gateway subject line.

The stored spellings follow the reference's demo data: the bare
enum-member names (PENDING/SUCCEEDED/REFUNDED, PAYMENT_CHANNEL_MOCK,
BALANCE/WECHAT/MOCK), mapped both ways at the service boundary.

verified over the live stack: the intent materializes the PENDING
ledger row off the seeded mock channel, the confirm answers
SUCCEEDED/first_success and the order reads PAID, and the replayed
confirm answers FailedPrecondition — the ledger replay can never
double-walk the order
